<section class="install-quickstart">
	<div class="callout callout-warning">
		<p>Do not run the installer as root. Run it as your normal user. It asks for <code>sudo</code> only when it needs it.</p>
	</div>

	<h2 id="requirements">Before you start</h2>
	<p>WavesHyprland deploys a rice onto an existing Arch Linux installation. It is not a full operating system or disk installer, so Arch must already be installed and working.</p>

	<h2 id="quick-install">Quick install</h2>
	<pre><code>git clone https://github.com/WavesOS-Repos/WavesHyprland.git
cd WavesHyprland
./install.sh --all</code></pre>

	<p>To pick steps interactively, run the installer with no flags:</p>
	<pre><code>./install.sh</code></pre>

	<p>To see verbose logs during the install:</p>
	<pre><code>WAVES_QUIET=0 ./install.sh --all</code></pre>

	<h2 id="installer-flags">Installer flags</h2>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Flag</th>
				<th>Action</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr><td><code>--all</code></td><td>Full install</td></tr>
			<tr><td><code>--yay</code></td><td>Install yay</td></tr>
			<tr><td><code>--packages</code></td><td>Install packages from pacman.txt and aur.txt</td></tr>
			<tr><td><code>--backup</code></td><td>Back up existing configs</td></tr>
			<tr><td><code>--configs</code></td><td>Deploy configs/</td></tr>
			<tr><td><code>--wallfliper</code></td><td>Deploy Wallfliper</td></tr>
			<tr><td><code>--themes</code></td><td>Install from themes/</td></tr>
			<tr><td><code>--sddm</code></td><td>Install the qylock SDDM theme and user helper</td></tr>
			<tr><td><code>--post</code></td><td>Set permissions, color seeds and the default wallpaper</td></tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<div class="callout callout-tip">
		<p>Back up anything you care about first. The installer can replace existing configs, and <code>--backup</code> keeps a copy of them.</p>
	</div>
</section>
